# List → Detail → Edit Pattern

When building CRUD views for entities (users, campaigns, etc.):

1. **List view** (`/dashboard/[entity]`) — Table with search/filter, rows link to detail
2. **Detail view** (`/dashboard/[entity]/[id]`) — Read-only display, Edit button links to edit
3. **Edit view** (`/dashboard/[entity]/[id]/edit`) — Self-contained form (UserForm pattern)

For nested entities (campaigns under users):

1. **List view** (`/dashboard/users/[id]/campaign`) — Table of campaigns, rows link to detail
2. **Detail view** (`/dashboard/users/[id]/campaign/[campaignId]`) — Single campaign read-only
3. **Edit view** (`/dashboard/users/[id]/edit/campaign/[campaignId]`) — Single campaign form
